WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:06.340
Peru holds about seventy percent of the world's tropical glaciers.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.820
Your satellite was built to watch them.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:20.960
Satellite records show that Andean glaciers have lost a large share of their ice since the 1970s.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:27.470
Their meltwater feeds rivers that millions of people depend on in the dry season.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:36.360
Clouds often hide the mountains, so scientists combine optical, thermal and radar data.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:43.810
NISAR, a radar satellite from NASA and India's space agency, maps ice and ground motion

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.320
through clouds, day and night.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:58.160
NISAR flies at 747 kilometres and sees the same ground every 12 days with a 12-metre antenna.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:04.240
You did it on a foundation budget. Small missions can still watch big changes.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:10.700
<v Chicho>My father herded alpacas under that ice. Now we measure it from space.

